{"id":"arpad","name":"Arpad","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:arpad"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Arpad","text":"(Isa. 10:9; 36:19; 37:13), also Arphad, support, a Syrian city near Hamath, along with which it is invariably mentioned (2 Kings 19:13; 18:34; Isa. 10:9), and Damascus (Jer. 49:23). After a siege of three years it fell (B.C. 742) before the Assyrian king Tiglath-pileser II. Now Tell Erfud."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H774","lemma":"אַרְפָּד","xlit":"ʼArpâd","gloss":"Arpad, a place in Syria","kjv":"Arpad, Arphad","count":3,"share":1},{"strong":"H5617","lemma":"סְפַרְוַיִם","xlit":"Çᵉpharvayim","gloss":"Sepharvites","kjv":"","count":3,"share":1},{"strong":"H2574","lemma":"חֲמָת","xlit":"Chămâth","gloss":"Chamath, a place in Syria","kjv":"Hamath, Hemath","count":3,"share":1},{"strong":"H2012","lemma":"הֵנַע","xlit":"Hênaʻ","gloss":"Hena, a place apparently in Mesopotamia","kjv":"Hena","count":2,"share":0.67},{"strong":"H5755","lemma":"עִוָּה","xlit":"ʻIvvâh","gloss":"Ivvah or Avva, a region of Assyria","kjv":"Ava, Ivah","count":2,"share":0.67},{"strong":"H8111","lemma":"שֹׁמְרוֹן","xlit":"Shômᵉrôwn","gloss":"Shomeron, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Samaria","count":2,"share":0.67}],"verses":["2Kgs.18.34","2Kgs.19.13","Isa.36.19"],"related":[{"id":"sepharvaim","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.5,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"ava","type":"lexical","strong":"H5617","why":"both lead with סְפַרְוַיִם (H5617)"},{"id":"sepharvaim","type":"lexical","strong":"H5617","why":"both lead with סְפַרְוַיִם (H5617)"}],"works":[]}
